>> title: Whitefish Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: smoked fish, mayonnaise, no-cook, appetizing, deli
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: smoked whitefish salad, chub salad, whitefish, whitefish spread, smoked fish salad
>> pairs-with: bagels, cream-cheese, scallion-schmear
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 20 min
>> slack: narrow — smoked fish and mayonnaise is a three-day item in the fridge and not a counter one, and the flakes go to paste if they are stirred
>> step.1: debone the whitefish, keep the flakes big
>> step.2: whisk the dressing
>> step.3: fold in the celery and dill
>> step.4: chill 2 hr

Skin @whole smoked whitefish{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; a golden chub from the fish case, bought smoked) and lift the meat off the frame in the largest pieces it will give you, going over every piece twice for pin bones.

Whisk @mayonnaise{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @sour cream{2%Tbs}, @lemon juice{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and @cayenne{1%pinch} together.

Fold @&(~1)dressing{} into @&(~2)picked whitefish{} with @celery{1%rib}(diced fine), @red onion{2%Tbs}(diced fine) and @fresh dill{2%Tbs}(chopped), turning it over just enough to coat.

Chill @&(~1)whitefish salad{} ~chill{2%hr}.
